      "rev_n_1_156850_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_156850_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_156850",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the parity of the sum of the sequence. If the sum is odd, BitLGM wins; if even, BitAryo wins.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446466.7546828
      },
      "rev_n_2_b28e01_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_b28e01_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_b28e01",
        "thought_text": "Consider the maximum value in the sequence. If there exists a number greater than the sum of all other numbers, BitLGM can force a win.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446466.7546911
      },
      "rev_n_3_3cf9e6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_3cf9e6_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_3cf9e6",
        "thought_text": "Evaluate the sequence for any zeros. If all numbers are zero, the game ends immediately, and BitAryo wins by default since BitLGM cannot make a move.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446466.754696
      },
      "rev_n_1_156850_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_156850_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_156850",
        "thought_text": "The current approach incorrectly assumes that the parity of the total sum determines the winner. Instead, the game's outcome depends on the Grundy numbers (or Nimbers) of the positions, which need to be calculated based on the possible moves available.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_156850_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_87dabe87a9",
        "created_at": 1791446474.6176379
      },
      "rev_n_1_156850_2": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_156850_2",
        "node_id": "n_1_156850",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in the way the Grundy numbers are calculated and combined. Specifically, the recursive calls to `grundy` within the loop for calculating Grundy values might be incorrect, leading to an incorrect overall Grundy number for the position. Instead, consider calculating the Grundy number for each position by considering both possible moves and using the minimum excludant (mex) of the resulting positions. This should ensure that the Grundy numbers are correctly computed for each state, allowing for accurate determination of the winning strategy.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_156850_1",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9ef4feffec",
        "created_at": 1791446489.175041
      }
